=== email subject
[End of life since 30 Sep 2026] Microsoft Windows Server 2016: security updates have stopped
=== email body
What's affected:
  Microsoft Windows Server, version 2016
  That is release 2016 on endoflife.date.

Why it matters:
  Security updates for Microsoft Windows Server 2016 stopped on 30 Sep 2026: newly found flaws in it, including ones attackers use, are not fixed any more. Extended support (often paid) is listed until 30 Sep 2029.

What to do:
  1. Upgrade to a supported release. The vendor's lifecycle page says which releases are supported; see https://endoflife.date/windows-server
  2. Until you can upgrade, limit who can reach it (for example, no access from the internet) and keep an eye on its vendor's advisories.

Links:
  endoflife.date: https://endoflife.date/windows-server

--
When you have dealt with it, run: patchtacio ack eol/microsoft-windows-server/2016
Patchtacio then stops reminding you about it.
You get this alert because Microsoft Windows Server is on your Patchtacio product list.
